[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2139948768","pull_request_review_id":2916836236,"id":2139948768,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_jQbg","diff_hunk":"@@ -143,6 +143,11 @@ class Node : public Object {\n \t\tPauseMode pause_mode : 2;\n \t\tPhysicsInterpolationMode physics_interpolation_mode : 2;\n \n+\t\t// Cached value, kept up to date when adding to tree, showing / hiding etc.\n+\t\t// This is shared for 2D and 3D, but the logic for propagating this flag in each case is different,\n+\t\t// for historical reasons.\n+\t\tbool visible_in_tree : 1;","path":"scene/main/node.h","commit_id":"54e5949ffb9f049fe36d10bb701e50658193cd52","original_commit_id":"9d2873072de6fd0c14a7adc2d80c2a063bd26316","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"You do discuss this in the OP, but I'm not sure I agree that _all_ nodes should have a \"visible\" flag.\r\n\r\nCurrently, we do a hard tree separation when a node isn't what's expected:\r\n`Node3D -> Node -> Node3D`\r\nIn this example, the leaf `Node3D` won't inherit transforms from the root `Node3D`, because a `Node` is between them.\r\n\r\nI'd argue that this is expected behavior in Godot. Propagating a singular property like `visible_in_tree` breaks this expectation.\r\nInstead, perhaps this property should be added to `Node2D` and `Node3D` separately?","created_at":"2025-06-11T11:57:25Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T12:02:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2139948768","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2139948768"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2139948768"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2139948768/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":149,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2139954677","pull_request_review_id":2916836236,"id":2139954677,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_jR31","diff_hunk":"@@ -293,7 +296,17 @@ class Spatial : public Node {\n \tbool is_visible() const;\n \tvoid show();\n \tvoid hide();\n-\tbool is_visible_in_tree() const;\n+\tbool is_visible_in_tree() const {\n+#if 0","path":"scene/3d/spatial.h","commit_id":"54e5949ffb9f049fe36d10bb701e50658193cd52","original_commit_id":"9d2873072de6fd0c14a7adc2d80c2a063bd26316","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"By 'optionally' you mean by changing to `#if 1`? I'm not sure we have dead regression testing code elsewhere in the codebase.","created_at":"2025-06-11T12:00:51Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T12:02:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2139954677","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2139954677"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2139954677"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2139954677/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":300,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":16,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140390100","pull_request_review_id":2917550637,"id":2140390100,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_k8LU","diff_hunk":"@@ -143,6 +143,11 @@ class Node : public Object {\n \t\tPauseMode pause_mode : 2;\n \t\tPhysicsInterpolationMode physics_interpolation_mode : 2;\n \n+\t\t// Cached value, kept up to date when adding to tree, showing / hiding etc.\n+\t\t// This is shared for 2D and 3D, but the logic for propagating this flag in each case is different,\n+\t\t// for historical reasons.\n+\t\tbool visible_in_tree : 1;","path":"scene/main/node.h","commit_id":"54e5949ffb9f049fe36d10bb701e50658193cd52","original_commit_id":"9d2873072de6fd0c14a7adc2d80c2a063bd26316","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I don't think (?) I've changed the existing behaviour, and I wasn't suggesting propagating between 3D / 2D nodes ... as I say in the notes that would be compat breaking so we are constrained by history here.\r\n\r\nNow we are using single bits the case is less convincing to have separate flags for the 2D / 3D line, unless it is to emphasize that their behaviour is different. We won't be saving any memory. I'd probably go the other way and share the `visible` flag in the `Node`.\r\n\r\nThis both reduces code duplication and leaves the opportunity for optimizations when traversing the tree. If we don't _know_ there is a flag, we have to query the node type each time through casting, which may be expensive. If we _know_ there is a flag we can always read it, even if it is say, always true in the case of `Node` that doesn't derive from `CanvasItem` or `Spatial`, and only take expensive casting branch when e.g. visible is `false`.","created_at":"2025-06-11T14:43:51Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T14:44:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140390100","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140390100"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140390100"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140390100/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":149,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2139948768,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140412250","pull_request_review_id":2917586500,"id":2140412250,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_lBla","diff_hunk":"@@ -293,7 +296,17 @@ class Spatial : public Node {\n \tbool is_visible() const;\n \tvoid show();\n \tvoid hide();\n-\tbool is_visible_in_tree() const;\n+\tbool is_visible_in_tree() const {\n+#if 0","path":"scene/3d/spatial.h","commit_id":"54e5949ffb9f049fe36d10bb701e50658193cd52","original_commit_id":"9d2873072de6fd0c14a7adc2d80c2a063bd26316","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I tend to add a lot of regression testing code in complex systems, see `SceneTreeFTI`, batching renderer, BVH.\r\nNormally I hide these behind clear defines, but in this case I thought it was kind of obvious how to enable it.\r\n\r\nWe can't always do unit testing (or external unit tests) for all situations and sometimes we need to catch regressions in the wild, so having switchable code that can easily track this down is preferable imo to just leaving later investigators blind to figuring out what is going on.\r\n\r\nOften, we can end up removing regression testing code after a couple of betas.\r\n\r\nAn alternative here would be to add the testing code as `#ifdef DEV_ENABLED` (and maybe make the detected bug more obvious, as it will probably go wrong in release).","created_at":"2025-06-11T14:52:38Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T14:52:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140412250","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140412250"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140412250"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140412250/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":300,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2139954677,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":16,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140424051","pull_request_review_id":2917606389,"id":2140424051,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_lEdz","diff_hunk":"@@ -293,7 +296,17 @@ class Spatial : public Node {\n \tbool is_visible() const;\n \tvoid show();\n \tvoid hide();\n-\tbool is_visible_in_tree() const;\n+\tbool is_visible_in_tree() const {\n+#if 0","path":"scene/3d/spatial.h","commit_id":"54e5949ffb9f049fe36d10bb701e50658193cd52","original_commit_id":"9d2873072de6fd0c14a7adc2d80c2a063bd26316","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I don't think I'm against it, even though I probably wouldn't do it myself. As long as you remember to remove it once it's in the clear :^)","created_at":"2025-06-11T14:57:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T14:57:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140424051","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140424051"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140424051"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140424051/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":300,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2139954677,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":16,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140431002","pull_request_review_id":2917617906,"id":2140431002,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_lGKa","diff_hunk":"@@ -143,6 +143,11 @@ class Node : public Object {\n \t\tPauseMode pause_mode : 2;\n \t\tPhysicsInterpolationMode physics_interpolation_mode : 2;\n \n+\t\t// Cached value, kept up to date when adding to tree, showing / hiding etc.\n+\t\t// This is shared for 2D and 3D, but the logic for propagating this flag in each case is different,\n+\t\t// for historical reasons.\n+\t\tbool visible_in_tree : 1;","path":"scene/main/node.h","commit_id":"54e5949ffb9f049fe36d10bb701e50658193cd52","original_commit_id":"9d2873072de6fd0c14a7adc2d80c2a063bd26316","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Oh, sorry, I totally missed that this continues to respect 3D / 2D boundaries.\r\n\r\nI think i'd still argue to separately store these values, since we'll otherwise attach them to a ton of `Node` objects that aren't visible. Even if it doesn't add storage, it adds some mental overhead. But yea, it does make this a lot less pressing. Let's see if someone else wants to weigh in.\r\n\r\n(If we're worried about this creating unnecessary duplicate logic, perhaps it's worth thinking about a `NodeVisible` / `NodeXD` / something else as a common superclass. I'm sure there's at least a bit of logic that could be consolidated.)","created_at":"2025-06-11T15:00:29Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T15:01:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140431002","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140431002"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140431002"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140431002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":149,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2139948768,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140613714","pull_request_review_id":2917920973,"id":2140613714,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_lyxS","diff_hunk":"@@ -143,6 +143,11 @@ class Node : public Object {\n \t\tPauseMode pause_mode : 2;\n \t\tPhysicsInterpolationMode physics_interpolation_mode : 2;\n \n+\t\t// Cached value, kept up to date when adding to tree, showing / hiding etc.\n+\t\t// This is shared for 2D and 3D, but the logic for propagating this flag in each case is different,\n+\t\t// for historical reasons.\n+\t\tbool visible_in_tree : 1;","path":"scene/main/node.h","commit_id":"54e5949ffb9f049fe36d10bb701e50658193cd52","original_commit_id":"9d2873072de6fd0c14a7adc2d80c2a063bd26316","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> (If we're worried about this creating unnecessary duplicate logic, perhaps it's worth thinking about a NodeVisible / NodeXD / something else as a common superclass. I'm sure there's at least a bit of logic that could be consolidated.)\r\n\r\nRan into a snag with this before with `CullInstance` in 3.x. It turns out when you derive from an extra class it appears in the Inspector in the editor (unless there is some way to prevent this?). This can end up being confusing for users.\r\n\r\nAnd this only solves the code duplication, it doesn't solve the performance issue of having to cast and branch for each node depending whether or not it actually has visibility flags. I do understand where you are coming from, but this _will_ cost FPS for some games (especially once we start bringing in some more scene tree optimizations), and a comment to explain the behaviour would do the job.\r\n\r\nI would argue for moving more common flags to `Node`, and have an explanation for the paradigm that not all flags are used on all `Nodes`.\r\n\r\nThis is already used for `_is_vi_visible()`. The flag is on `Spatial` rather than `VisualInstance` for the same reason, it means no casting is (in theory) required prior to using the flag. However because non-VI `Spatial` can also be hidden, that's why I wanted to move to a more encompassing system that handles all cases without casting.\r\n\r\nAlso worth noting:\r\n`_is_visible_in_tree()` on the `Node` is an internal function. It isn't intended to be exposed to users, and is wrapped by `is_visible_in_tree()` in `Spatial` (and later potentially in `CanvasItem`). The outward facing paradigm is the same, only the internal data organization is different here.\r\n\r\n","created_at":"2025-06-11T16:23:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T16:27:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140613714","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140613714"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140613714"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140613714/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":149,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2139948768,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140836779","pull_request_review_id":2918309034,"id":2140836779,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_mpOr","diff_hunk":"@@ -293,7 +296,17 @@ class Spatial : public Node {\n \tbool is_visible() const;\n \tvoid show();\n \tvoid hide();\n-\tbool is_visible_in_tree() const;\n+\tbool is_visible_in_tree() const {\n+#if 0","path":"scene/3d/spatial.h","commit_id":"54e5949ffb9f049fe36d10bb701e50658193cd52","original_commit_id":"9d2873072de6fd0c14a7adc2d80c2a063bd26316","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Have changed it to `DEV_ENABLED` and made it more obvious.\r\n\r\nWe'll get roughly the same speed as before in `DEV` builds and it should spot any regressions, and can remove this code after beta testing.","created_at":"2025-06-11T18:36:52Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T18:36:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140836779","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140836779"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107324#discussion_r2140836779"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107324"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2140836779/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":300,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2139954677,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":16,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2142129557","pull_request_review_id":2920189538,"id":2142129557,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_rk2V","diff_hunk":"@@ -732,6 +735,36 @@ Ref<World> Spatial::get_world() const {\n \treturn data.viewport->find_world();\n }\n \n+void Spatial::_update_visible_in_tree() {\n+\tSpatial *parent = get_parent_spatial();\n+\n+\tbool propagate_visible = parent ? parent->data.visible_in_tree : true;\n+\n+\t// Only propagate visible when entering tree if we are visible.\n+\tpropagate_visible &= is_visible();\n+\n+\t_propagate_visible_in_tree(this, propagate_visible);\n+}\n+\n+void Spatial::_propagate_visible_in_tree(Spatial *p_node, bool p_visible_in_tree) {","p